* 1n4148.lib - onsemi 1N4148, small-signal switching diode, DO-204AH
* (DO-35).
* VENDOR MODEL, COPIED VERBATIM FROM THE MANUFACTURER'S OWN FILE.
*
* USAGE:
*   .include models/diodes/1n4148.lib
*   D1 anode cathode D1N914
*
* Role in this project: TWO instances form the negative-rail bias
* reference of the gain block (circuits/preamp/gain_block.py:252-253),
* footprint FP_DO35. It is the only diode in the signal-path bias chain,
* and before L24 nobody had ever verified it - ADR-016 lists it as "mai
* verificato".
*
* ======================================================================
* READ THIS BEFORE YOU "FIX" ANY OF THE THREE NAMES
* ======================================================================
*
* THE PART IS THE 1N4148. THE FILE THIS IS DERIVED FROM IS CALLED
* 1n914.lib. THE MODEL INSIDE IS CALLED D1N914. All three are correct.
*
* onsemi files the 1N4148 under the 1N914 document: its product page for
* the 1N4148 links exactly one datasheet, and that datasheet is
* 1n914-d.pdf. The model file says so itself, in its own header:
*
*   ** Product: 1N/FDLL914/A/B / 916/A/B / 4148 / 4448
*   ** Package: DO-35 / LL-34
*
* AND THE FILE THAT LOOKS RIGHT IS THE WRONG ONE.
* https://www.onsemi.com/download/models/lib/1n4148.lib returns HTTP 200,
* application/octet-stream, a REAL 1189-byte file - containing
* .SUBCKT 1N4148WT, which is the SOD-323 variant, not the DO-35 this
* project uses. ngspice loads it without a word and simulates a different
* device. The same bytes are served as 1n4148wt.lib, which is what proves
* it is an alias rather than a server typo.
*
* That is docs/limitations.md #20, and it is the reason this file's name
* was chosen for the PART (1n4148.lib, what circuits/ instantiates)
* while the model name inside was left exactly as the vendor wrote it.
* Do not "correct" either one. The full record is in
* models/diodes/1n4148.provenance.json.
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* PROVENANCE - the short version. Freeze in
* vendor/diodes/onsemi/1N4148/PROVENANCE.json, reasoning in ADR-017 and
* docs/preamp/reports/2026-09-10-L24-t7-dispositivi-attivi.md
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
*
* THE PART WAS NOT SUBSTITUTED, IT WAS ATTRIBUTED. 1N4148 is a generic
* industry type number, not one manufacturer's part, so T7 (ADR-016) is
* satisfied not by replacing the device but by naming the manufacturer
* whose model and lifecycle statement the project stands on. That
* manufacturer is onsemi: it publishes both a reachable SPICE model and
* an explicit Active status (six OPN, all Active, read from the product
* page's own JSON-LD). Vishay serves a more recent datasheet but no SPICE
* model to a non-browser client.
*
* Frozen byte-for-byte at vendor/diodes/onsemi/1N4148/1n914.lib and
* copied here unchanged - nothing removed, no value rounded, reordered or
* "corrected". The Fairchild Semiconductor attribution line at the bottom
* is the vendor's own and is reproduced unaltered.
*
*   diff <(grep -v '^\*' vendor/diodes/onsemi/1N4148/1n914.lib) \
*        <(grep -v '^\*' models/diodes/1n4148.lib)      # empty
*
* Note the model's own creation stamp: Jul-24-2007, Rev 1.0. Like the two
* MJE models, this is old, and it is the newest thing the manufacturer
* publishes.
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* CROSS-CHECKED AGAINST THE DATASHEET - BOTH PUBLISHED LIMITS INSIDE
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
*
* Datasheet 1N914/D, September 2024 Rev. 6, frozen at
* vendor/diodes/onsemi/1N4148/1n914-d.pdf. The 1N4148 row, not the 914B
* row - they differ. ngspice 47, set temp = 25:
*
*   V_F @ I_F = 10 mA         0.766187 V   1.0 V MAX.   INSIDE (23% margin)
*   C_T @ V_R = 0, 1 MHz      0.8687 pF    4.0 pF MAX.  INSIDE
*
* Both re-measured in L25 and both reproduce L24 to the digit.
*
* WORTH KNOWING RATHER THAN COMFORTING: C_T sits 4.6x BELOW the
* guaranteed ceiling. The model therefore describes a typical or better
* specimen, not the worst case the datasheet permits. For a bias diode at
* 1 mA that does not matter; in a signal path it would.
*
* At the actual working point the model gives V_F = 0.631952 V at 1 mA,
* where the datasheet specifies nothing.
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* A LIVE EXAMPLE OF limitations.md #19, IN THIS VERY DATASHEET
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
*
* onsemi's document toolchain renders the micro prefix in a way that
* pdftotext extracts as the letter m, silently and with exit 0. In
* 1n914-d.pdf the reverse-current row at VR = 20 V, TA = 150 C reads
* "50 mA" in the extracted text and 50 uA on the rendered page - wrong by
* a factor of 1000, and perfectly plausible either way.
*
* Neither of the two limits locked above is affected (10 mA and 4.0 pF
* are both above the milliamp boundary and were read on the render), but
* any current limit below a milliamp in this document must be LOOKED AT,
* not extracted.
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* WHAT THIS MODEL DOES NOT HAVE
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
*
* NO FLICKER NOISE: no KF, no AF. In this repo only models/jfet/lsk489.lib
* has 1/f noise (NC-004). It also carries no temperature coefficients
* beyond EG and the built-in defaults, and no reverse-recovery beyond
* TT = 1.012e-8.
*
* No SPICE magnitude suffix appears anywhere in the model, so
* docs/limitations.md #13 has nothing to bite on here.
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* BELOW THIS LINE: THE VENDOR FILE, BYTE FOR BYTE
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
****** Power Discrete Diode Electrical Parameters ******
** Product: 1N/FDLL914/A/B / 916/A/B / 4148 / 4448
** Package: DO-35 / LL-34
**------------------------------------------------------
.MODEL D1N914 D
+ IS=3.45e-09
+ RS=0.452422
+ IKF=0.0528
+ N=1.94
+ ISR=1.01e-09
+ NR=2.0
+ CJO=8.68e-13
+ M=0.02504
+ VJ=0.90906
+ FC=0.5
+ TT=1.012e-8
+ BV=100 
+ IBV=1e-05
+ EG=0.92
**------------------------------------------------------
